<GuideLayout 
  title="OEM vs. ODM: Which Manufacturing Path Is Right for Your Scale-Up?" 
  type="STRATEGY"
  description="Understanding the core differences between custom design (OEM) and private labeling (ODM) to optimize your brand's growth strategy."
>
  <h2>Decoding Manufacturing Models</h2>
  <p>As a <strong>Supply Chain Partner</strong>, we often help brands decide between OEM and ODM paths. Choosing the right one can significantly impact your <strong>Inventory Management</strong> and initial ROI.</p>

  <h3>OEM (Original Equipment Manufacturing)</h3>
  <p>Ideal for established brands with unique tech packs. We provide full custom development, sourcing proprietary fabrics, and creating custom molds for every detail. This path offers maximum differentiation in competitive markets like the US and UK.</p>

  <h3>ODM (Original Design Manufacturing)</h3>
  <p>Perfect for brands looking for a "Ready-to-Ship" strategy. You select from our 450,000 PCS monthly stock, and we apply your private label. This drastically reduces lead times and allows for lower MOQ testing of new trends.</p>

  <h3>The Fitclo Hybrid Approach</h3>
  <p>Most of our successful partners use a hybrid model: ODM for core basics to ensure stable <strong>Inventory Management</strong>, and OEM for their "Hero" products to establish market authority. Our <strong>Global Logistics</strong> team ensures both paths are consolidated into seamless international shipments.</p>
</GuideLayout>
